Modifications made in this image relative to the upstream m1k1o/neko base:
  - Replaced the bundled frontend with a demodesk-based build (native touch,
    auto-login, embed/cast modes).
  - Patched neko.yaml (implicit_hosting).
  - §AI-control: disabled neko's built-in Chromium launch; the shared browser is
    now launched and driven by @playwright/mcp (Playwright launch/pipe transport);
    added Node.js, @playwright/mcp, a bundled open-source Chromium, and supervisord
    programs (browser-mcp, browser-keeper). Removed the CDP socat proxy.

Chromium is used under its own (BSD-style) open-source license; the browser binary
installed here is Playwright's bundled open-source Chromium (not Google Chrome).

